WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.567
Talk of

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:01.601
the potential danger

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.770
China poses to the United States.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.705
Beijing is a top focus

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:05.972
of the

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.474
annual Senate Intelligence Committees

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.509
hearing on worldwide threats

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:10.844
That hearing offers

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:11.945
a rare opportunity

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.913
for the public to hear directly

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.715
from the US intel leaders,

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.484
and their message was simple

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:18.184
and aggressive.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.688
China will not back down

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.024
The People's Republic of China,

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.625
which is increasingly challenging

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.559
the United States

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.328
economically, technologically,

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.096
politically and militarily.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.464
Around the world, remains

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.433
our unparalleled priority.

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.100
President Xi

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.169
Jinping will continue efforts

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:38.972
to achieve Xi's vision of making China

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.174
the preeminent power in East Asia.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.743
And a major power on the world stage.

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.678
To fulfill Xi's vision,

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:46.713
however, the CCP

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.481
is increasingly convinced

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.416
that it can only do

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.017
so at the expense of U.S.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.185
power and influence.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.189
And joining me now is CNN global affairs

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:56.790
analyst Kim

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.725
Dozier and retired Lieutenant General

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.226
Mark Hertling.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:00.960
He's a military

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.095
analyst and former

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.263
commanding general of the U.S.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.432
Army Europe and Seventh Army.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:06.332
So, Kim,

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:06.933
that quote,

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.969
China remains our unparalleled priority.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:11.938
That's really significant,

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.373
especially in the context

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.507
this week of China

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.543
basically warning the United States

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:18.611
to tone down the rhetoric.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.980
But it almost seems as if both sides

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.582
are denying their role

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.818
in kind of the spiraling of tensions

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:25.785
between the two.

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:26.286
And the U.S.

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:27.153
intelligence community

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.255
is not backing down

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.158
Absolutely.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:32.492
The U.S.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.194
intelligence community

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:37.197
years back felt like nobody was listening

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.065
to their repeated warnings

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:42.902
about Beijing's expansion and intentions

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.971
of expansion in terms of military,

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.506
their military intelligence

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:47.607
and also things

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.609
like their influencing operations,

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:50.810
trying to influence

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.579
what Americans think about China,

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.481
but about their own government.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.648
And that's where they really got

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:56.883
into the hole.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.918
You know, warnings about TikTok

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.321
and how it can feed certain messages

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.122
to U.S.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.824
audiences to influence opinion.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.360
And now the intelligence community

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.128
really feels like,

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.096
okay, we've got your attention

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.397
The spy balloon helped.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:12.899
And we're going to lay out for you

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.968
all the different ways that this is

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.404
a national enterprise for China

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:19.305
to eventually become

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.940
the premier world power.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.675
And that means taking back

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:23.877
Taiwan eventually,

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.044
hopefully not by force

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.880
from Beijing's perspective,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.714
but that it's something

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.082
that bears watching

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.050
and that it is their job

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.085
to keep watching

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.120
and warning the White House about it.

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.889
And General Hertling,

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.357
the tensions between the U.S.

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:37.924
and China,

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.692
it would be no exaggeration to say

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.827
it's the highest it's

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.795
been in many, many years.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:43.429
The director

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:44.597
of National Intelligence, Avril

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:44.998
Haines, said

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.966
that China will continue its efforts

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.035
to undercut the United States

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.905
But as a military person, how concerned

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.606
are you that that actually could spiral

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.542
into a kinetic conflict,

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:57.010
a military conflict between these

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:57.777
two countries?

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.280
Well, you know,

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:00.980
what I would

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.282
suggest is the report

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.783
that the DNI puts out

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.018
is relatively short.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.219
It's unclassified.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.354
It's ten chapters and 40 pages

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.056
and they address that.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:10.423
In fact,

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.258
there's a great line from the report,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.092
if I can remember,

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:13.893
off the top of my head,

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.262
it said Beijing is increasingly combining

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.598
their growing military power

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.667
with an economic, technological

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.569
and diplomatic influence

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:23.670
to not only strengthen

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.973
the party in China, but to pursue

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.675
regional preeminence and pursue

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.143
global influence.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:32.612
That, to me is problematic.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:35.548
Director Haines has a very good point.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:38.051
With all the other intelligence officials

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:40.553
saying that it should be the priority.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.355
But truthfully, Abby,

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.523
what I'd also say

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:47.060
is it's a short and long term priority.

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.429
We have to address some of the key issues

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.097
now that China is doing there.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:52.699
Advances in wireless

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:54.867
communications, semiconductors,

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:55.501
quantum

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.970
is synthetic biology,

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.072
which I had to look up to understand.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.707
But at the same time,

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:03.176
I was commander in Europe in 2011

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:05.211
when the Obama administration said

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.513
we need to pivot our attention

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:10.817
to the East, to Asia, to China.

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:11.985
And what happened

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:14.153
was we started paying less attention

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:15.655
to countries like Russia.

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:18.224
And we see where that got us in 2014.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.193
So this DNI report,

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.028
which is relatively short,

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:22.996
really addresses

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:24.464
all the key factors

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.299
that the intelligence community

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.333
has to watch.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:27.900
And truthfully,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.569
I've been reading these for years.

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:31.504
This is the most complex

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.006
and complicated one

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:34.707
I've seen because of

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.442
the amount of challenges

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:39.412
and threats that the United States faces

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:41.547
today, more so than ever before.

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:43.683
And can you keep this up?

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:44.717
Just a moment ago,

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.519
the FBI director, Chris Wray,

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.521
raised his national security concerns

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:49.822
about ticktock. Take a listen.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.159
Could the

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:54.027
Chinese government,

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:56.229
through its ownership of bytedance

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.797
that owns bytedance us

00:04:57.797 --> 00:04:58.865
if they wanted to

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.500
and bytedance us

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.434
were willing to cooperate

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.568
or forced to cooperate,

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:03.002
could they

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:05.338
could they use TikTok to control data

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:08.174
on millions of users?

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:09.542
Yes.

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.144
Could they use it to control

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.912
the software on millions of devices,

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:14.914
given the opportunity to do so? Yes.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.850
Could they use it to drive narratives

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.085
like to divide Americans

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.953
against each other, for example,

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.489
let's say China wants to invade Taiwan to

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:25.058
make sure that Americans

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:26.826
are seeing videos arguing

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:29.228
why Taiwan belongs to China, why the U.S.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.430
should not intervene.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.331
Yes,

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.200
I think a lot of Americans

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.835
who have TikTok on their phone wonder,

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:38.037
is this being blown out of proportion

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.941
I think a lot of people

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.810
don't realize that

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:45.078
President Xi,

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:45.611
he did

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.180
what may sound like a very boring thing.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.348
Back in 2017,

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:50.049
he changed Chinese law

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:52.618
to give the government access

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:55.555
to all private companies, data

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:57.390
programing, etc.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.858
So that means

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.060
and also he made all Chinese companies

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.163
cooperate with

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.599
military companies and technology

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:07.567
if needed.

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:10.069
So that means that Beijing can ostensibly

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.838
tell bytedance

00:06:11.838 --> 00:06:13.639
you're going to show us your code,

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:14.941
you're going to show us your data,

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.743
you're going to change your code,

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:18.311
and you're going to let us send

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:19.412
certain messages out.

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.213
Even though I know

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.347
the owners of Bytedance

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:22.849
pushed back against that.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:25.585
That is still technically the possibility

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.153
under this 2017

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:29.088
policy change that you made.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:31.290
And you heard also there

00:06:32.225 --> 00:06:33.693
the FBI director making the point

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:35.828
that in China, the line between public

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:36.763
and private entities

00:06:36.763 --> 00:06:37.663
is just not the same

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:39.465
as what we're used to here

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:40.833
in the United States.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:41.534
We have to leave it there.

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:43.436
Kim Dozier and General Mark Hertling,

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:44.837
both of you, thank you very much.

